    "result_text": "Only `AcceptanceTest` contains tests (the other files are the base class and support). All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field so the API returns `SILVER` when an owner's `namesakeCount` is `0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing pattern for derived read-only fields (like `membershipNumber`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` enum property (`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `MembershipTierEnum` and the JSON field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression plus a `membershipTier(Owner)` helper that returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and email is non-blank, else `BRONZE`.\n\nVerification:\n- Project compiles (`mvnw compile`), and the generated DTO exposes `membershipTier` as expected.\n- Full test suite green: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 covering both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (BRONZE).",
